      "id": "claim_166796e41f454ff6a7303eb82739be67",
      "statement": "The structured logger enforces the no-secrets rule in the type system: ReservedLogField bans field names like body, header(s), message, prompt, secret, and token in both logger defaults and call details (only component and the event/error pair are exempt), loggers are created with fixed dot-separated component metadata plus package-owned field vocabularies, and every call emits one indexed object with a concrete event name and caught values passed as error.",
      "evidence": [
